sentences.l:
and not easily could it
with both hands a man hold, not even one quite in youthful prime,
such as mortals now are;

and he, from above, cast it in, lifting it,
and it smashed the four-ridged helmet, and the bones it crushed together,
all of them together, of the head;

yet all the same he did not forget the joy of battle,
but he, Thestor’s-son Alcmaon with his spear having hit,
stabbed him, and drew out the spear;

And him Ajax and Teucer, going together, the one with an arrow
had struck, the strap about his chest, shining,
of the man-covering shield;

and Hector, snatching up a stone, carried it, which before the gates
had stood, thick at the base, but above
it was sharp;

and it not two men, the best of the people,
easily onto a wagon from the ground could heave up,
such as mortals now are;

And he stood, going very near, and bracing himself struck them in the middle,
standing well astride, so that for him the missile might not be the weaker,
and tore off both hinges;

and he shone with bronze
frightful, which he wore about his skin, and two
spears in his hands he held;
